x549 text "A program is a list of functions. A function is a header `fn NAME T... -> T`, then one instruction per line `ID OP ARGS`, then `ret ARG` (or `ret OP ARGS`, which names a fresh node), then `end`. Names are lowercase identifiers. Parameters are p0, p1, ... in header order. An argument is an earlier ID in the same function, a parameter, a u32 literal, true, or false. There are no forward references, no recursion, and no nested expressions."
