x660 text "Views and edits"
x661 puts x659 x660
x662 call close x661 
x663 call open x662 2
x664 write x663 2
x665 text "A model never sees a whole file. It asks for a view of one function: the function with a handle line on top (e0), one signature line per callee, and a program handle (g0). The program view is scoped to the target, its transitive callees and its direct callers, so it stays the same size as the program grows. The revision is a short hash of the program text; an edit written against an older revision is rejected rather than applied to code that has moved. A reply is the handle line followed by edits, one per line, as in the quick start."
x666 puts x664 x665
x667 call close x666 
x668 call open x667 10
x669 write x668 4
x670 write x669 2
